The upstream project is a Discord adapter for DeepSeek Harness. This fork:

- renames the package to @aporb/dsh-discord while keeping the plugin row id and
  settings namespace `dsh-discord`;
- pins the dependency matrix to the DeepSeek Harness desktop 0.2.2-rc.1 host
  line and adapts the host face to it (live deltas from `assistant-stream`
  frames, projection title translation, current session-list signature);
- is an English-only build: one locale file, no language setting;
- adds a mention-driven workspace/conversation picker, bound-channel attach,
  `/session pick`, conversation-title sync for Discord threads, a visible
  turn-failure line, and a one-time token/allowlist bootstrap from a legacy
  bot env file (`DSH_DISCORD_BOOTSTRAP_ENV`, default `~/.hermes/.env`);
- removes the upstream CI, marketplace artifacts, and Chinese documentation.

